@@ -148,6 +148,22 @@ Every option is optional except `password`. The `name` option is worth calling o
 > [!NOTE]
 > The `secure: true` option tells the browser to only store and send the cookie over HTTPS. When developing locally over plain HTTP, compliant browsers (notably Safari and iOS, and Chrome on some local domains) silently drop the cookie, so the session will not persist. Set `cookie: { secure: false }` during local development to work around this.
 
+## Rotating the password
+
+To change `password` without signing everyone out, set the new one as `password` and keep the previous one in `extraUnsealPasswords`:
+
+```ts
+const session = await useSession(event, {
+  password: process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_NEW!,
+  extraUnsealPasswords: [process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_OLD!],
+});
+```
+
+- Extra passwords only open sessions. Sealing always uses `password`.
+- A session opened with an extra password is resealed with `password`, even on a request that only reads it. As with `idleTimeout`, this can overlap with a concurrent write and the write may be lost.
+- Extra passwords need the same minimum length as `password`. They are validated when sealing (`useSession` for a new session, `updateSession`, `sealSession`), not when only reading.
+- Remove old passwords once the rotation period is over, and keep the list short: each extra password adds a PBKDF2 derivation for cookies that no password opens, and a leaked old password stays valid while listed.
+
 ## Expiration
 
 Sessions have two independent expiration controls, and you can use either or both:
